Package: katten
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         libkf6wallet6,
         plasma-workspace,
         qml6-module-org-kde-kirigami,
         qml6-module-qtquick-controls
Recommends: kwalletmanager
Description: Unofficial Mistral Vibe client for KDE Plasma
 Katten is a Qt-native Kirigami application for KDE Plasma 6 that lets you
 chat with Mistral AI's Vibe using your own API key, without a web browser.
 .
 Features:
  * Full multi-turn conversations via the Mistral Conversations API
  * Rich-text answers (bold, lists, tables, links, code blocks, charts)
  * Optional web search through Mistral's built-in web_search tool
  * API key stored securely in KWallet, never in plain text
  * Optional KRunner plugin in the separate katten-krunner package
 .
 Katten is not affiliated with Mistral AI. Using the Mistral API requires
 an API key from console.mistral.ai and may incur costs.

Package: katten-krunner
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         katten,
         plasma-workspace
Description: KRunner plugin for Katten (Mistral Vibe)
 This package adds a KRunner plugin that sends prompts typed in KRunner
 (Alt+Space), e.g. "katten <question>", to the Katten application over D-Bus.
